00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.030
This video, I'm going to give you a short
demonstration on how to use some of the

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.100
basic text editing tools within Word.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.080
For this example, I've already
written a letter that I'm going to

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.950
send to one of the team members.

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:18.960
And in the letter, the first thing I need
to do is I need to add the address, now

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.730
I have the address in another document.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:28.770
So if I open that document, I can
highlight the employee's name and address.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.380
I can then go up to the toolbar and
select copy or alternatively press the

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.630
Control and C buttons, that will copy
that information onto  the clipboard,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.580
I can then go back to the letter.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:47.580
Place my curosr where I wish to insert
it and then select the paste option.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.280
And I am keeping the text only.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.400
Once that is in there, I can then
continue formatting the letter.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.930
I have a paragraph here that
I wish to change around.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.379
So this paragraph here, I'm
going to move to the bottom.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.150
This time, I need to actually
copy the information in such a

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.090
way that it disappears from one
place and reappears in the other.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.230
So to do that, I use the Cut tool.

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:19.320
So if I click on the scissor icon, that
will cut the information from there.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.620
I then just need to place my
cursor where I wish to enter it.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.540
And then again, select
paste, and click paste.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.600
That then inserts it where I want to.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.300
I press the enter key just to
give a line space between that.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:39.060
If I wasn't happy with that, if you look
at the top tool bar, you can see there

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:42.240
is small icon, which is undo typing.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.580
So I click on that, that will undo what
I have done and I click it again and

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.289
it will take that information back out.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:55.650
If I want to put it back in, I can click
on the redo and that will redo the text.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.590
So each step that you wish to
go back, you can click on that.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:03.630
And if you want to redo it, you will
then be able to redo the information.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:12.020
There are occasions where you may wish
to change a word within a document.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.530
So for this example, I'm going
to select the word "team".

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.740
As you can see, there are several
instances of the word team.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.770
I've just going to demonstrate
by selecting that word.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.280
So I have got team and what
I wish to do is replace.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.660
So I click the replace.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.360
It will ask me what is I want to replace.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:29.960
So.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.100
I need to find the word "team".

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.109
I'm going to replace it with "group".

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.710
So there's two options here.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.040
I can replace all or
replace one at a time.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.730
The thing to remember here is to
be careful with this, because if

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:52.140
they are words that you select to
replace that are part of another

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.850
word, it will change those.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.369
So in this instance, I'm
just going to select replace.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.620
So that's automatically highlighting
the instances for replace.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.630
If I click replace it will change
it from the replace to group.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.030
Again, replace to group.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:13.460
And as I clicked through it has changed
at every instance of the word Team.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.070
Once that's completed, I can close that.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.740
And as you can see all of the
instances of "team" have been

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.500
changed to the word "group".

